  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 131 PM CDT Sun May 31 2026\n\nMid-level ridging will be in place through Monday, weakening as we \nhead through the upcoming week. We'll start to see an increase in \ndeep moisture over the next couple of days. This should allow for a \nfew sea breeze showers and storms by Tuesday afternoon. As a mid-\nlevel low developed of the southern California coast and ridging \nshifts a bit east, we'll open up a stream of Pacific moisture \nthat should increase rain chances at least a bit Wednesday through\nFriday with medium (40-50%) chances these days. While most of the\nactivity this week will likely be an enhanced sea breeze variety,\nby late week the shifting ridge and approaching mid-level low \ncould support some eastward movement of convection that develops \nover the high terrain of Mexico. Friday into Saturday will be the \nbest potential for this as the aforementioned mid-level low kicks\nout across the region. \n\nHigh temperatures remain mainly near normal levels throughout the \nupcoming week. Elevated surface humidity levels combined with this \nwill mean heat index values in the upper 90s to just above 100 \ndaily. Heat risk levels will be low to moderate most days.",
